# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local dev (see README "Local dev over HTTPS")
#
# Dev does NOT run on localhost: Google matches OAuth redirect URIs exactly and
# the client is registered for
#   https://dev.tokyoluckycard.com:5173/auth/callback/google
# so the dev origin must be that one. Two prerequisites:
#   1. dev.tokyoluckycard.com resolves to 127.0.0.1 (Cloudflare DNS-only A
#      record, or an /etc/hosts entry)
#   2. `yarn certs` has generated ./certs (mkcert)
#
# Vite proxies /api to the Go service, so VITE_SERVER_URL is this same origin:
# an https page may not call http://localhost:3000 (mixed content), and going
# same-origin also drops CORS and keeps session cookies first-party.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SERVER_URL=https://dev.tokyoluckycard.com:5173
VITE_WEBSITE_URL=https://dev.tokyoluckycard.com:5173

# Production (Railway): the web app and the API are separate origins on the
# same registrable domain, which keeps SuperTokens cookies same-site.
#   VITE_SERVER_URL=https://api.tokyoluckycard.com
#   VITE_WEBSITE_URL=https://app.tokyoluckycard.com

# SuperTokens API base path — must match apiBasePath in tlc-service
# (pkg/supertokens/supertokens.go).
VITE_ST_API_BASE_PATH=/api/auth

# Public resource directory
VITE_ASSETS_DIR=

# Stripe publishable key (Stripe.js loaded from CDN, never bundled)
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset bucket — MinIO locally, Railway Bucket in prod. Same bucket the Go
# service writes card images to (its BUCKET_PUBLIC_URL), reused for the
# background music track so audio is never bundled into the JS.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Relative in dev, so it resolves against the dev origin and goes through the
# /bucket proxy above — an https page may not load http://localhost:9000 at all.
#
# In prod, point it at the bucket's public presigner. Note that host implies the
# bucket, so the name is NOT in the path — /music/main-theme.mp3 resolves,
# /card-images/music/main-theme.mp3 404s. The /bucket proxy rewrites the local
# path-style prefix to match, so the app uses one relative key in both.
#
#   VITE_BUCKET_URL=https://s3-public-presigner-production-c74c.up.railway.app
VITE_BUCKET_URL=/bucket
